/*  The stash machine — `src/Interpreter/StashTransform.cs` and `StashTypeSubstitution.cs`.

    ★ Once checking is over, every burying function becomes two: a RESUME function holding the body
    as a machine of steps — basic blocks, a step counter, a slot for every local that has to outlive
    a resumption — and a FACTORY of the original name, which makes the state and hands back a
    closure over it. Then every written `stash of T` becomes the closure it lowers to: nothing in,
    `voidable T` out. `stashing.cufe` has already refused what cannot be split, so nothing here
    refuses but a local whose type was never recorded.

    ★ Built the way C# builds it, node for node, so the program handed on is the same tree: a
    machine's every node stands at the burying function's own line and column, but a bury's
    `Return` and a for-each's own pieces keep theirs.

    ⚠ A machine is an object, and an object is copied when handed on — so everything it changes
    lives in its series and maps, which are shared: the blocks, each block's statements, exit and
    guards, the guards in force, and the counter for invented names.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// A basic block: what it runs, how it leaves (empty until set — the first exit wins), and the
    /// conditions that were true on the way in, re-tested when it is assembled to restore narrowing.
    Define object stash-block with (the series of node body, the series of node leaving, the series of node guards).

    /// One burying body being turned into steps.
    Define object machine with (the node burying, the text key, the text owner, the node row, the node col,
        the series of stash-block blocks, the series of node guards-now, the map from text to node invented,
        the map from text to number counts, the map from text to node locals).

    // ── Nodes the machine writes ──────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node to machine-number, given (the number amount):
        Return cast made on ("NumberLiteral", a series with (cast numeral on (amount))).
    Done.

    Bind node to machine-var unto machine, given (the text name):
        Return cast made on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on (name), one's row, one's col)).
    Done.

    Bind node to machine-define unto machine, given (the text name, the node value):
        Return cast made on ("DefineStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (name), value, cast flag on (false),
            cast flag on (false), one's row, one's col, cast nothing)).
    Done.

    Bind node to machine-binary unto machine, given (the node left, the text op, the node right):
        Return cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (left, cast atom on (op), right, one's row, one's col)).
    Done.

    Bind node to machine-return-void unto machine:
        Return cast made on ("ReturnStatement", a series with (cast made on ("VoidLiteral", a series with (one's row, one's col)),
            one's row, one's col)).
    Done.

    Bind node to machine-if, given (the node condition, the node body, the node otherwise-body):
        Define arms as cast listed.
        Cast arms's add on (cast made on ("ConditionArm", a series with (condition, body))).
        Return cast made on ("IfStatement", a series with (arms, otherwise-body)).
    Done.

    Bind node to machine-list, given (the series of node items):
        Return a new node { the kind "list", the word "", the children items }.
    Done.

    /// The step assignment: `stash_frame`'s one item becomes `goes-to`.
    Bind node to machine-set-step unto machine, given (the number goes-to):
        Return cast made on ("SeriesSetStatement", a series with (cast one's machine-var on ("stash_frame"),
            cast machine-number on (1), cast machine-number on (goes-to), one's row, one's col)).
    Done.

    Bind node to machine-branch unto machine, given (the node condition, the number when-true, the number when-false):
        Return cast machine-if on (condition, cast machine-list on (a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (when-true))),
            cast machine-list on (a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (when-false)))).
    Done.

    // ── Blocks ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// A new block, holding the guards in force now — a copy, unaffected by what is pushed later.
    Bind number to machine-new-block unto machine:
        Define held as a series of node.
        For each guard in one's guards-now, repeat:
            Insert guard into held.
        Done.
        Insert a new stash-block { the body a series of node, the leaving a series of node, the guards held } into one's blocks.
        Return the number of one's blocks - 1.
    Done.

    /// Block `at`, counted from 0 as C# counts its steps.
    Bind stash-block to machine-block unto machine, given (the number at):
        Return item (at + 1) of one's blocks.
    Done.

    /// The first exit wins: a block that already left is not left again by what contained it.
    Bind void to machine-set-exit unto machine, given (the number at, the series of node leaving):
        Define block as cast one's machine-block on (at).
        If the number of block's leaving is greater than 0, return.
        For each statement in leaving, repeat:
            Insert statement into block's leaving.
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind void to machine-add unto machine, given (the number at, the node statement):
        Insert statement into (cast one's machine-block on (at))'s body.
    Done.

    // ── Linearising ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Emits `statements` from block `current`, and says which block carries on. `continue-to` and
    /// `break-to` are the enclosing loop's steps, or -1 outside one.
    Bind number to machine-emit unto machine, given (the node statements, the number current,
            the number continue-to, the number break-to):
        Define at as current.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            Define splits as cast contains-bury on (statement) or kind is "StopStatement" or kind is "SkipStatement".
            If splits is false and break-to is not -1, the splits becomes cast has-free-loop-exit on (statement).
            If splits, the at becomes cast one's machine-control on (statement, at, continue-to, break-to).
            Otherwise, cast one's machine-add on (at, statement).
        Done.
        Return at.
    Done.

    /// An arm's body with `guard` in force for the block it starts in and every block made inside.
    Bind number to machine-emit-guarded unto machine, given (the node body, the number entry,
            the number continue-to, the number break-to, the node guard):
        If cast is-nothing on (guard), return cast one's machine-emit on (body, entry, continue-to, break-to).
        Insert guard into (cast one's machine-block on (entry))'s guards.
        Insert guard into one's guards-now.
        Define reached as cast one's machine-emit on (body, entry, continue-to, break-to).
        Remove item (the number of one's guards-now) from one's guards-now.
        Return reached.
    Done.

    /// Does this condition narrow what it tests — `is a`, or `is not void` — not looking into a nested function?
    Bind fact to narrows-a-type, given (the node tree):
        If tree's kind is "atom" or tree's kind is "BindStatement" or tree's kind is "LambdaLiteral", return false.
        If tree's kind is "IsTypeCheck", return true.
        If tree's kind is "BinaryExpression" and (cast field-of on (tree, 2))'s word is "NotEqual":
            If (cast field-of on (tree, 1))'s kind is "VoidLiteral" or (cast field-of on (tree, 3))'s kind is "VoidLiteral", return true.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            If cast narrows-a-type on (child), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    Bind number to machine-control unto machine, given (the node statement, the number current,
            the number continue-to, the number break-to):
        Judge statement's kind, where it is:
            "BuryStatement":
                Define next as cast one's machine-new-block.
                Cast one's machine-set-exit on (current, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (next),
                    cast made on ("ReturnStatement", a series with (cast field-of on (statement, 1),
                        cast field-of on (statement, 2), cast field-of on (statement, 3))))).
                Return next.
            Done.
            "IfStatement", return cast one's machine-if-statement on (statement, current, continue-to, break-to).
            "JudgeStatement", return cast one's machine-judge on (statement, current, continue-to, break-to).
            "WhileStatement":
                Define header as cast one's machine-new-block.
                Define body as cast one's machine-new-block.
                Define past as cast one's machine-new-block.
                Cast one's machine-set-exit on (current, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (header))).
                Cast one's machine-set-exit on (header, a series with (cast one's machine-branch on (cast field-of on (statement, 1), body, past))).
                Define tail as cast one's machine-emit on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), body, header, past).
                Cast one's machine-set-exit on (tail, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (header))).
                Return past.
            Done.
            "RepeatUntilStatement":
                // The test has a block of its own, so a `Skip` lands on the until-check.
                Define body as cast one's machine-new-block.
                Define test as cast one's machine-new-block.
                Define past as cast one's machine-new-block.
                Cast one's machine-set-exit on (current, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (body))).
                Define tail as cast one's machine-emit on (cast field-of on (statement, 1), body, test, past).
                Cast one's machine-set-exit on (tail, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (test))).
                Cast one's machine-set-exit on (test, a series with (cast one's machine-branch on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), past, body))).
                Return past.
            Done.
            "ForEachStatement", return cast one's machine-for-each on (statement, current, continue-to, break-to).
            "StopStatement":
                Cast one's machine-set-exit on (current, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (break-to))).
                Return cast one's machine-new-block.
            Done.
            "SkipStatement":
                Cast one's machine-set-exit on (current, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (continue-to))).
                Return cast one's machine-new-block.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Return current.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    Bind number to machine-if-statement unto machine, given (the node statement, the number current,
            the number continue-to, the number break-to):
        Define arms as (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children.
        Define past as cast one's machine-new-block.
        Define entries as a series of number.
        For each arm in arms, repeat:
            Insert cast one's machine-new-block into entries.
        Done.
        Define otherwise-at as cast one's machine-new-block.
        Define dispatch-arms as cast listed.
        Define place as 0.
        For each arm in arms, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Cast dispatch-arms's add on (cast made on ("ConditionArm", a series with (cast field-of on (arm, 1),
                cast machine-list on (a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (item place of entries)))))).
        Done.
        Cast one's machine-set-exit on (current, a series with (cast made on ("IfStatement", a series with (dispatch-arms,
            cast machine-list on (a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (otherwise-at))))))).
        The place becomes 0.
        For each arm in arms, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define guard as cast nothing.
            If cast narrows-a-type on (cast field-of on (arm, 1)), the guard becomes cast field-of on (arm, 1).
            Define tail as cast one's machine-emit-guarded on (cast field-of on (arm, 2), item place of entries, continue-to, break-to, guard).
            Cast one's machine-set-exit on (tail, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (past))).
        Done.
        // The else arm narrows by elimination — expressible with exactly one arm that tests a type.
        Define else-guard as cast nothing.
        If the number of arms is 1:
            Define only as cast field-of on (item 1 of arms, 1).
            If only's kind is "IsTypeCheck":
                The else-guard becomes cast made on ("IsTypeCheck", a series with (cast field-of on (only, 1), cast field-of on (only, 2),
                    cast flag on (cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (only, 3)) is false), cast field-of on (only, 4), cast field-of on (only, 5))).
            Done.
        Done.
        Define otherwise-body as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body), the otherwise-body becomes cast listed.
        Define tail as cast one's machine-emit-guarded on (otherwise-body, otherwise-at, continue-to, break-to, else-guard).
        Cast one's machine-set-exit on (tail, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (past))).
        Return past.
    Done.

    /// `it is a A or it is a B …` at an arm's place, or the judgement's when there is no arm.
    Bind node to machine-any-of unto machine, given (the series of node cases, the node at-row, the node at-col):
        Define test as cast made on ("IsTypeCheck", a series with (cast one's machine-var on ("it"), item 1 of cases,
            cast flag on (false), at-row, at-col)).
        Define place as 1.
        While place is less than the number of cases, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            The test becomes cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (test, cast atom on ("Or"),
                cast made on ("IsTypeCheck", a series with (cast one's machine-var on ("it"), item place of cases,
                    cast flag on (false), at-row, at-col)), at-row, at-col)).
        Done.
        Return test.
    Done.

    /// An arm's dispatch test: its cases, or for a value arm, `it` equal to one of its values.
    Bind node to machine-arm-test unto machine, given (the node arm):
        If cast is-value-arm on (arm) is false:
            Return cast one's machine-any-of on ((cast field-of on (arm, 1))'s children, cast field-of on (arm, 3), cast field-of on (arm, 4)).
        Done.
        Define test as cast nothing.
        For each value in (cast field-of on (arm, 5))'s children, repeat:
            Define equal as cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (cast one's machine-var on ("it"), cast atom on ("Equal"),
                value, cast field-of on (arm, 3), cast field-of on (arm, 4))).
            If cast is-nothing on (test), the test becomes equal.
            Otherwise:
                The test becomes cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (test, cast atom on ("Or"), equal,
                    cast field-of on (arm, 3), cast field-of on (arm, 4))).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return test.
    Done.

    Bind number to machine-judge unto machine, given (the node statement, the number current,
            the number continue-to, the number break-to):
        // `it` becomes an ordinary local, evaluated once here and restored from its slot after.
        Cast one's machine-add on (current, cast one's machine-define on ("it", cast field-of on (statement, 1))).
        Define arms as (cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children.
        Define past as cast one's machine-new-block.
        Define entries as a series of number.
        For each arm in arms, repeat:
            Insert cast one's machine-new-block into entries.
        Done.
        Define otherwise-at as cast one's machine-new-block.
        Define otherwise-body as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
        // The leftover an `Otherwise` is reached for: the subject's cases the arms did not take.
        Define else-guard as cast nothing.
        Define valued as false.
        If the number of arms is greater than 0, the valued becomes cast is-value-arm on (item 1 of arms).
        If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body) is false and valued is false:
            Define subject-type as the entry for "it" in one's locals.
            If subject-type is not void:
                Define residue as a series of node.
                For each subject-case in (cast field-of on (subject-type, 1))'s children, repeat:
                    Define taken as false.
                    For each arm in arms, repeat:
                        For each arm-case in (cast field-of on (arm, 1))'s children, repeat:
                            If cast same-type on (arm-case, subject-case), the taken becomes true.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                    If taken is false, insert subject-case into residue.
                Done.
                If the number of residue is greater than 0:
                    The else-guard becomes cast one's machine-any-of on (residue, cast field-of on (statement, 4), cast field-of on (statement, 5)).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define dispatch-arms as cast listed.
        Define place as 0.
        For each arm in arms, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Cast dispatch-arms's add on (cast made on ("ConditionArm", a series with (cast one's machine-arm-test on (arm),
                cast machine-list on (a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (item place of entries)))))).
        Done.
        Cast one's machine-set-exit on (current, a series with (cast made on ("IfStatement", a series with (dispatch-arms,
            cast machine-list on (a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (otherwise-at))))))).
        The place becomes 0.
        For each arm in arms, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define guard as cast nothing.
            If cast is-value-arm on (arm) is false:
                The guard becomes cast one's machine-any-of on ((cast field-of on (arm, 1))'s children, cast field-of on (arm, 3), cast field-of on (arm, 4)).
            Done.
            Define tail as cast one's machine-emit-guarded on (cast field-of on (arm, 2), item place of entries, continue-to, break-to, guard).
            Cast one's machine-set-exit on (tail, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (past))).
        Done.
        If cast is-nothing on (otherwise-body), the otherwise-body becomes cast listed.
        Define tail as cast one's machine-emit-guarded on (otherwise-body, otherwise-at, continue-to, break-to, else-guard).
        Cast one's machine-set-exit on (tail, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (past))).
        Return past.
    Done.

    /// `For each x in xs` becomes an indexed `While`, so the loop's place is a number the frame holds.
    Bind number to machine-for-each unto machine, given (the node statement, the number current,
            the number continue-to, the number break-to):
        Define fe-row as cast field-of on (statement, 4).
        Define fe-col as cast field-of on (statement, 5).
        Define fresh as the entry for "fresh" in one's counts but void is 0.
        In one's counts, the entry for "fresh" becomes fresh + 1.
        Define source as "stash_source_{fresh}".
        Define index as "stash_index_{fresh}".
        In one's invented, the entry for source becomes the entry for "{fe-row's word}:{fe-col's word}" in one's invented but void is cast unknown-type.
        In one's invented, the entry for index becomes cast plain-type on ("NumberType").
        Define iterator as "it".
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) is false, the iterator becomes cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Cast one's machine-add on (current, cast one's machine-define on (source, cast field-of on (statement, 2))).
        Cast one's machine-add on (current, cast one's machine-define on (index, cast machine-number on (1))).
        Define header as cast one's machine-new-block.
        Define body as cast one's machine-new-block.
        Define step-at as cast one's machine-new-block.
        Define past as cast one's machine-new-block.
        Cast one's machine-set-exit on (current, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (header))).
        Define in-range as cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (cast one's machine-var on (index), cast atom on ("Lte"),
            cast made on ("SeriesLength", a series with (cast one's machine-var on (source), fe-row, fe-col)), fe-row, fe-col)).
        Cast one's machine-set-exit on (header, a series with (cast one's machine-branch on (in-range, body, past))).
        Cast one's machine-add on (body, cast one's machine-define on (iterator, cast made on ("SeriesAccess",
            a series with (cast one's machine-var on (source), cast one's machine-var on (index), fe-row, fe-col)))).
        Define tail as cast one's machine-emit on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), body, step-at, past).
        Cast one's machine-set-exit on (tail, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (step-at))).
        Cast one's machine-add on (step-at, cast made on ("BecomesStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (index),
            cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (cast one's machine-var on (index), cast atom on ("Plus"),
                cast machine-number on (1), fe-row, fe-col)), fe-row, fe-col))).
        Cast one's machine-set-exit on (step-at, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (header))).
        Return past.
    Done.

    // ── Hoisting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Any appearance of the name — read, reassigned or declared — anywhere inside.
    Bind fact to machine-mentions, given (the node tree, the text name):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return false.
        If tree's kind is "VariableReference" or tree's kind is "BecomesStatement" or tree's kind is "DefineStatement":
            If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)) is name, return true.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            If cast machine-mentions on (child, name), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    Bind fact to machine-writes, given (the node tree, the text name):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return false.
        If tree's kind is "BecomesStatement" and cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)) is name, return true.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            If cast machine-writes on (child, name), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    Bind fact to machine-mentions-in, given (the series of node statements, the text name):
        For each statement in statements, repeat:
            If cast machine-mentions on (statement, name), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// The names that must survive a resumption, in slot order, each as `[type "name"]`: a parameter
    /// the body reassigns, then every local declared at the top of a block.
    Bind series of node or failure to machine-hoisted unto machine:
        Define ordered as a series of node.
        Define seen as a map from text to fact.
        Define body as cast field-of on (one's burying, 4).
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (one's burying, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
            If cast machine-writes on (body, name) and (the entry for name in seen) is void:
                In seen, the entry for name becomes true.
                Insert parameter into ordered.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each block in one's blocks, repeat:
            For each statement in block's body, repeat:
                If statement's kind is "DefineStatement":
                    Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                    If (the entry for name in seen) is void:
                        In seen, the entry for name becomes true.
                        Define local-type as the entry for name in one's invented.
                        If local-type is void, the local-type becomes the entry for name in one's locals.
                        If local-type is void:
                            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{one's key}' buries, and the type of '{name}' could not be worked out", "",
                                cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)), "keep '{name}' across a bury",
                                "Everything that survives a resumption is stored, and storing it needs its type. Give it a starting value whose type is clear.")).
                        Done.
                        Insert cast machine-list on (a series with (local-type, cast quoted on (name))) into ordered.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return ordered.
    Done.

    Bind fact to machine-needs-load, given (the stash-block block, the text name):
        If cast machine-mentions-in on (block's guards, name), return true.
        For each statement in block's body, repeat:
            If cast machine-mentions on (statement, name):
                If statement's kind is not "DefineStatement", return true.
                Return cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) is not name.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return cast machine-mentions-in on (block's leaving, name).
    Done.

    Bind fact to machine-changes, given (the stash-block block, the text name):
        For each statement in block's body, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "DefineStatement" and cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) is name, return true.
            If cast machine-writes on (statement, name), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// Writes a local back to its slot — filling the slot if this is the first write.
    Bind node to machine-store unto machine, given (the text name):
        Define slot as cast one's machine-var on ("stash_slot_{name}").
        Define empty as cast one's machine-binary on (cast made on ("SeriesLength", a series with (slot, one's row, one's col)),
            "Equal", cast machine-number on (0)).
        Define fill as cast made on ("SeriesInsertStatement", a series with (cast one's machine-var on (name),
            cast one's machine-var on ("stash_slot_{name}"), cast nothing, cast flag on (false), one's row, one's col)).
        Define overwrite as cast made on ("SeriesSetStatement", a series with (cast one's machine-var on ("stash_slot_{name}"),
            cast machine-number on (1), cast one's machine-var on (name), one's row, one's col)).
        Return cast machine-if on (empty, cast machine-list on (a series with (fill)), cast machine-list on (a series with (overwrite))).
    Done.

    /// One block: load what it reads, run it, write back what it changed, then leave — inside its guards.
    Bind series of node to machine-assemble unto machine, given (the stash-block block, the series of node hoisted):
        Define result as a series of node.
        For each held in hoisted, repeat:
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (held, 2)).
            If cast machine-needs-load on (block, name):
                Insert cast one's machine-define on (name, cast made on ("SeriesAccess", a series with (
                    cast one's machine-var on ("stash_slot_{name}"), cast machine-number on (1), one's row, one's col))) into result.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define inner as a series of node.
        For each statement in block's body, repeat:
            Insert statement into inner.
        Done.
        For each held in hoisted, repeat:
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (held, 2)).
            If cast machine-changes on (block, name), insert cast one's machine-store on (name) into inner.
        Done.
        For each statement in block's leaving, repeat:
            Insert statement into inner.
        Done.
        Define back as the number of block's guards.
        While back is greater than 0, repeat:
            Define guarded-one as cast machine-if on (item back of block's guards, cast machine-list on (inner),
                cast machine-list on (a series with (cast one's machine-return-void))).
            The inner becomes a series of node with (guarded-one).
            Decrement back by 1.
        Done.
        For each statement in inner, repeat:
            Insert statement into result.
        Done.
        Return result.
    Done.

    // ── Building ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The resume function and the factory, in that order.
    Bind series of node or failure to machine-build unto machine:
        Define entry as cast one's machine-new-block.
        Define tail as cast one's machine-emit on (cast field-of on (one's burying, 4), entry, -1, -1).
        Cast one's machine-set-exit on (tail, a series with (cast one's machine-set-step on (the number of one's blocks))).

        Define hoisted as cast one's machine-hoisted or pass the failure off.
        Define hoisted-names as a map from text to fact.
        For each held in hoisted, repeat:
            In hoisted-names, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (held, 2)) becomes true.
        Done.
        Define passed as a series of node.
        Define parameter-names as a map from text to fact.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (one's burying, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
            In parameter-names, the entry for name becomes true.
            If (the entry for name in hoisted-names) is void, insert parameter into passed.
        Done.
        Define burying-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (one's burying, 1)).
        Define yields as cast made on ("VoidableType", a series with (cast field-of on (one's burying, 2))).
        Define resume-name as "stash_resume_{burying-name}".

        Define resume-parameters as cast listed.
        Cast resume-parameters's add on (cast machine-list on (a series with (
            cast made on ("SeriesType", a series with (cast plain-type on ("NumberType"))), cast quoted on ("stash_frame")))).
        For each held in hoisted, repeat:
            Cast resume-parameters's add on (cast machine-list on (a series with (
                cast made on ("SeriesType", a series with (cast field-of on (held, 1))),
                cast quoted on ("stash_slot_{cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (held, 2))}")))).
        Done.
        For each parameter in passed, repeat:
            Cast resume-parameters's add on (parameter).
        Done.

        // The dispatch: a loop over the step, one arm a block.
        Define spent as cast one's machine-return-void.
        Define dispatch-arms as cast listed.
        Define step as 0.
        For each block in one's blocks, repeat:
            Cast dispatch-arms's add on (cast made on ("ConditionArm", a series with (
                cast one's machine-binary on (cast one's machine-var on ("stash_step"), "Equal", cast machine-number on (step)),
                cast machine-list on (cast one's machine-assemble on (block, hoisted))))).
            Increment step by 1.
        Done.
        Define looped as cast machine-list on (a series with (
            cast one's machine-define on ("stash_step", cast made on ("SeriesAccess", a series with (
                cast one's machine-var on ("stash_frame"), cast machine-number on (1), one's row, one's col))),
            cast made on ("IfStatement", a series with (dispatch-arms, cast machine-list on (a series with (spent)))))).
        Define dispatch as cast machine-list on (a series with (
            cast made on ("WhileStatement", a series with (cast made on ("BooleanLiteral", a series with (
                cast flag on (true), one's row, one's col)), looped)),
            spent)).
        Define resume as cast made on ("BindStatement", a series with (cast quoted on (resume-name), yields, resume-parameters,
            dispatch, cast nothing, cast nothing, one's row, one's col)).

        // The factory: make the state, hand back a closure over it.
        Define factory-body as cast listed.
        Cast factory-body's add on (cast one's machine-define on ("stash_frame", cast made on ("SeriesLiteral", a series with (
            cast machine-list on (a series with (cast machine-number on (0))), cast plain-type on ("NumberType"), one's row, one's col)))).
        For each held in hoisted, repeat:
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (held, 2)).
            Define starting as cast listed.
            If (the entry for name in parameter-names) is not void, cast starting's add on (cast one's machine-var on (name)).
            Cast factory-body's add on (cast one's machine-define on ("stash_slot_{name}", cast made on ("SeriesLiteral",
                a series with (starting, cast field-of on (held, 1), one's row, one's col)))).
        Done.
        Define resume-arguments as cast listed.
        If one's owner is not "", cast resume-arguments's add on (cast one's machine-var on ("one")).
        Cast resume-arguments's add on (cast one's machine-var on ("stash_frame")).
        For each held in hoisted, repeat:
            Cast resume-arguments's add on (cast one's machine-var on ("stash_slot_{cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (held, 2))}")).
        Done.
        For each parameter in passed, repeat:
            Cast resume-arguments's add on (cast one's machine-var on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)))).
        Done.
        Define resumed as cast made on ("CastExpression", a series with (cast one's machine-var on (resume-name), resume-arguments,
            one's row, one's col)).
        Define closure as cast made on ("LambdaLiteral", a series with (cast listed,
            cast machine-list on (a series with (cast made on ("ReturnStatement", a series with (resumed, one's row, one's col)))),
            one's row, one's col)).
        Cast factory-body's add on (cast made on ("ReturnStatement", a series with (closure, one's row, one's col))).
        Define factory as cast made on ("BindStatement", a series with (cast field-of on (one's burying, 1),
            cast made on ("FunctionType", a series with (cast listed, yields)), cast field-of on (one's burying, 3),
            factory-body, cast nothing, cast nothing, one's row, one's col)).
        Return a series of node with (resume, factory).
    Done.

    /// A machine for one burying body, its locals as the checker recorded them under `key`.
    Bind series of node or failure to built-machine unto checker, given (the node burying, the text key, the text owner):
        Define locals as a map from text to node.
        Define prefix as "{key}\t".
        For each pair in one's stash-locals, repeat:
            If the key of pair starts with prefix:
                In locals, the entry for (the characters from (the length of prefix + 1) to the end of the key of pair) becomes the value of pair.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define invented as a map from text to node.
        For each pair in one's series-loops, repeat:
            In invented, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define building as a new machine { the burying burying, the key key, the owner owner,
            the row cast field-of on (burying, 7), the col cast field-of on (burying, 8),
            the blocks a series of stash-block, the guards-now a series of node, the invented invented,
            the counts a map from text to number, the locals locals }.
        Return cast building's machine-build or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    // ── Where machines go (`StashTransform.Rewrite`) ──────────────────────

    /// The statements with every burying body replaced by its machine — reached the way C# reaches them.
    Bind node or failure to with-machines unto checker, given (the node statements):
        Define rewritten as cast listed.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            If kind is "BindStatement":
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 5).
                Define body as cast field-of on (statement, 4).
                If cast contains-bury on (body):
                    Define owner as "".
                    Define key as name.
                    If cast is-nothing on (target) is false:
                        The owner becomes cast unquoted on (target).
                        The key becomes "{owner}'s {name}".
                    Done.
                    Define pair-built as cast one's built-machine on (statement, key, owner) or pass the failure off.
                    For each made-one in pair-built, repeat:
                        // An `unto` method keeps its `unto`, both halves.
                        If owner is not "", cast rewritten's add on (cast with-field on (made-one, 5, target)).
                        Otherwise, cast rewritten's add on (made-one).
                    Done.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Cast rewritten's add on (cast with-field on (statement, 4, cast one's with-machines on (body) or pass the failure off)).
                Done.
            Done.
            Otherwise if kind is "PullStatement" or kind is "PullRabbitStatement":
                Cast rewritten's add on (cast with-field on (statement, 2,
                    cast one's with-machines on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off)).
            Done.
            Otherwise if kind is "ObjectDefinition":
                Define owner as cast def-name on (statement).
                Define methods as cast listed.
                For each method in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
                    Define method-body as cast field-of on (method, 4).
                    If cast contains-bury on (method-body):
                        Define pair-built as cast one's built-machine on (method, "{owner}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1))}", owner)
                            or pass the failure off.
                        For each made-one in pair-built, repeat:
                            Cast methods's add on (made-one).
                        Done.
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        Cast methods's add on (cast with-field on (method, 4, cast one's with-machines on (method-body) or pass the failure off)).
                    Done.
                Done.
                Cast rewritten's add on (cast with-field on (statement, 4, methods)).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast rewritten's add on (statement).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return rewritten.
    Done.

    /// Does anything in the program bury — a function or a method, anywhere?
    Bind fact to anything-buries, given (the node tree):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return false.
        If tree's kind is "BindStatement" and cast contains-bury on (cast field-of on (tree, 4)), return true.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            If cast anything-buries on (child), return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// Every `For each` over a stash replaced, where it stands, by the drain it was checked as.
    Bind void to place-drains unto checker, given (the node tree):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return.
        Define place as 0.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define drain as cast unknown-type.
            If child's kind is "ForEachStatement":
                Define spot as "{(cast field-of on (child, 4))'s word}:{(cast field-of on (child, 5))'s word}".
                Define held as the entry for spot in one's stash-drains.
                If held is not void, the drain becomes held.
            Done.
            If cast is-none on (drain), cast one's place-drains on (child).
            Otherwise:
                Cast rewrite-field on (tree, place, drain).
                Cast one's place-drains on (drain).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    // ── Written stash types (`StashTypeSubstitution`) ─────────────────────

    /// Every `stash of T` replaced, where it stands, by the closure it lowers to — never looking
    /// inside an object type, which is nominal and may hold itself.
    Bind void to substitute-stash-types, given (the node tree):
        If tree's kind is "atom" or tree's kind is "ObjectType", return.
        Define place as 0.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Cast substitute-stash-types on (child).
            If child's kind is "StashType":
                Cast rewrite-field on (tree, place, cast made on ("FunctionType", a series with (cast listed,
                    cast made on ("VoidableType", a series with (cast field-of on (child, 1)))))).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// What the checker hands on once stashes are lowered: drains in place, machines built, written
    /// stash types substituted. Nothing changes in a program where nothing buries.
    Bind node or failure to lowered-stashes unto checker, given (the node handed, the node written):
        If the size of one's stash-drains is greater than 0, cast one's place-drains on (handed).
        If cast anything-buries on (written) is false, return handed.
        Define built as cast one's with-machines on (handed) or pass the failure off.
        Cast substitute-stash-types on (built).
        Return built.
    Done.
Done.
